  "kernel_repo": "Aiden-HQ/AidenHQ",
  "notes": [
    "May add authority (grants, writes, roles or secrets) in: agent-builder, ai-reviewer, apps-platform, chief-of-staff, clickhouse, code-review, design, engineering, fleet-steward. Auto-updates accept it; turn them off to review first.",
    "A repo review starts all its checks at once; deepsec setup PR gets a conventional title and its .gitignore",
    "Briefs carry open calls with defaults; multi-task code work links one spec",
    "Two clear setup options and the Slack app made from a config token",
    "Aiden passes the owner's words to the Researcher",
    "One clear Google setup, Desktop clients only",
    "Calendar writes and Gmail drafts, sends and labels behind review",
    "Intake owns incoming Slack, Primer and meeting action items",
    "The Steward is the fleet's operator",
    "Searchable model picker and a redesigned repo review form",
    "Hybrid AI task search over the warehouse",
    "Spend and source-completeness outcome checks",
    "Agent anatomy — local modules, agent memory, shared skills, event routines, sharing",
    "Self-filling projects, the board as the one approvals UI, richer waiting and scheduled cards",
    "Cap per-push review rounds (push_rounds, default 1)",
    "Install security updates automatically, reboot stays manual",
    "Answers and reminders survive delivery failures; Fast chat attachments; drawer save errors",
    "GitHub service survives a failed repo read, Slack reconcile keeps live messages, and two more review fixes",
    "Re-run a wedged check run's job and report a head the merge gate holds",
    "Name a new Slack app after the instance so bot handles don't collide"
  ],
  "release": "2026.11.24"
}
